---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { CALL_HREF } from "../../siteConfig";

const title = "Why your AI keeps forgetting you — and the simple fix";
const description = "Every session starts from scratch. Here's why — and the 15-minute fix that most people never bother to set up.";
const date = "June 26, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title={`${title} — Nrvana AI`} description={description}>
  <section class="section pt-20 pb-6">
    <div class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest" style="color: var(--color-accent-deep);">Memos · Individual</div>
    <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight max-w-3xl">
      {title}
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm" style="color: var(--color-ink-mute);">{date}</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section py-10">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>You open a new chat. You type your question. The AI helps you. You close the window.</p>
      <p>Next day, same thing — except the AI has no idea who you are. You explain yourself again. Your industry, your role, your writing style, what you're trying to build.</p>
      <p>This happens every time. It's not a glitch. It's how these tools work by default.</p>
      <p>Here's why — and the 15-minute fix.</p>

      <h2>Why sessions start from zero</h2>
      <p>AI chat tools are stateless by design. Each new conversation begins with a blank slate. The model isn't building a picture of you over time the way a good colleague would — it starts fresh with every chat.</p>
      <p>For a one-off question, this is fine. But if you use AI for real work — drafting, thinking, planning, researching — you burn a surprising amount of time just re-establishing context. Who you are. How you like to communicate. What you're working on. What you never want.</p>
      <p>That's friction. And it compounds.</p>

      <h2>The fix: a file about you</h2>
      <p>The simplest thing you can do is write a short document — two paragraphs, a bullet list — that describes you. Then paste it into any AI chat before you start working.</p>
      <p>We call it a Soul File. Your version might cover:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Who you are.</strong> Your role, industry, what kind of work you actually do each day.</li>
        <li><strong>Your voice.</strong> How you like things written. "Direct and brief" vs. "warm and thorough" vs. "dry and precise."</li>
        <li><strong>Your no-list.</strong> What you never want the AI to suggest or assume. ("Don't recommend I hire anyone." "Assume I'm writing for a non-technical audience.")</li>
        <li><strong>What's in focus right now.</strong> The project, goal, or problem currently top of mind.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Write it once. Use it across every tool — Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini, Cursor, all of them.</p>

      <h2>What changes when you have one</h2>
      <p>The AI stops treating you like a stranger. You stop spending the first five minutes of every session catching it up. You get straight to the work.</p>
      <p>Small thing. Outsized difference — especially if you're using AI daily.</p>

      <h2>If you'd rather not build it alone</h2>
      <p>This is one of the five things we hand you in our <a href="/services/snapshot">Acceleration Snapshot</a>. It's also the centerpiece of our <a href="/services/personal-cortex">Personal Cortex Setup</a>, where we build the full version around you — with memory, context templates, and two installed workflows — over five to seven days.</p>
      <p><a href={CALL_HREF}>Start with a free 30-minute call</a> if you'd like to figure out which one fits better. No pitch, just a conversation about where your time goes.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section py-16">
    <div class="rounded-2xl p-10 text-center" style="background-color: var(--color-ink); color: var(--color-canvas);">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Ready to stop re-explaining yourself?</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a href="/services/snapshot" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-6 py-3 font-medium"
           style="background-color: var(--color-canvas); color: var(--color-ink);">
          See the Snapshot — $450
        </a>
        <a href={CALL_HREF} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-6 py-3 underline underline-offset-4"
           style="color: var(--color-canvas-soft);">
          Book a free 30-minute call
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section py-8">
    <a href="/memos" class="text-sm underline underline-offset-4" style="color: var(--color-ink-mute);">← All memos</a>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
